#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:96
msgid "safeLoad (string [ , options ])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:98
msgid ""
"**Recommended loading way.** Parses `string` as single YAML document. "
"Returns either a plain object, a string or `undefined`, or throws "
"`YAMLException` on error. By default, does not support regexps, functions"
" and undefined. This method is safe for untrusted data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:102 ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:170
msgid "options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:104
msgid ""
"`filename` _(default: null)_ - string to be used as a file path in "
"error/warning messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:106
msgid ""
"`onWarning` _(default: null)_ - function to call on warning messages. "
"Loader will call this function with an instance of `YAMLException` for "
"each warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:108
msgid "`schema` _(default: `DEFAULT_SAFE_SCHEMA`)_ - specifies a schema to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:109
msgid ""
"`FAILSAFE_SCHEMA` - only strings, arrays and plain objects: "
"http://www.yaml.org/spec/1.2/spec.html#id2802346"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:111
msgid ""
"`JSON_SCHEMA` - all JSON-supported types: "
"http://www.yaml.org/spec/1.2/spec.html#id2803231"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:113
msgid ""
"`CORE_SCHEMA` - same as `JSON_SCHEMA`: "
"http://www.yaml.org/spec/1.2/spec.html#id2804923"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:115
msgid ""
"`DEFAULT_SAFE_SCHEMA` - all supported YAML types, without unsafe ones "
"(`!!js/undefined`, `!!js/regexp` and `!!js/function`): "
"http://yaml.org/type/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:118
msgid "`DEFAULT_FULL_SCHEMA` - all supported YAML types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:119
msgid ""
"`json` _(default: false)_ - compatibility with JSON.parse behaviour. If "
"true, then duplicate keys in a mapping will override values rather than "
"throwing an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:121
msgid ""
"NOTE: This function **does not** understand multi-document sources, it "
"throws exception on those."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:124
msgid ""
"NOTE: JS-YAML **does not** support schema-specific tag resolution "
"restrictions. So, the JSON schema is not as strictly defined in the YAML "
"specification. It allows numbers in any notation, use `Null` and `NULL` "
"as `null`, etc. The core schema also has no such restrictions. It allows "
"binary notation for integers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:130
msgid "load (string [ , options ])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:132
msgid ""
"**Use with care with untrusted sources**. The same as `safeLoad()` but "
"uses `DEFAULT_FULL_SCHEMA` by default - adds some JavaScript-specific "
"types: `!!js/function`, `!!js/regexp` and `!!js/undefined`. For untrusted"
" sources, you must additionally validate object structure to avoid "
"injections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:145
msgid "safeLoadAll (string [, iterator] [, options ])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:147
msgid ""
"Same as `safeLoad()`, but understands multi-document sources. Applies "
"`iterator` to each document if specified, or returns array of documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:159
msgid "loadAll (string [, iterator] [ , options ])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:161
msgid "Same as `safeLoadAll()` but uses `DEFAULT_FULL_SCHEMA` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:164
msgid "safeDump (object [ , options ])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:166
msgid ""
"Serializes `object` as a YAML document. Uses `DEFAULT_SAFE_SCHEMA`, so it"
" will throw an exception if you try to dump regexps or functions. "
"However, you can disable exceptions by setting the `skipInvalid` option "
"to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:172
msgid "`indent` _(default: 2)_ - indentation width to use (in spaces)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:173
msgid ""
"`noArrayIndent` _(default: false)_ - when true, will not add an "
"indentation level to array elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:174
msgid ""
"`skipInvalid` _(default: false)_ - do not throw on invalid types (like "
"function in the safe schema) and skip pairs and single values with such "
"types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:176
msgid ""
"`flowLevel` (default: -1) - specifies level of nesting, when to switch "
"from block to flow style for collections. -1 means block style everwhere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:178
msgid "`styles` - \"tag\" => \"style\" map. Each tag may have own set of styles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:179
msgid "`schema` _(default: `DEFAULT_SAFE_SCHEMA`)_ specifies a schema to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:180
msgid ""
"`sortKeys` _(default: `false`)_ - if `true`, sort keys when dumping YAML."
" If a function, use the function to sort the keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:182
msgid "`lineWidth` _(default: `80`)_ - set max line width."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:183
msgid ""
"`noRefs` _(default: `false`)_ - if `true`, don't convert duplicate "
"objects into references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:184
msgid ""
"`noCompatMode` _(default: `false`)_ - if `true` don't try to be "
"compatible with older yaml versions. Currently: don't quote \"yes\", "
"\"no\" and so on, as required for YAML 1.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:186
#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"`condenseFlow` _(default: `false`)_ - if `true` flow sequences will be "
"condensed, omitting the space between `a, b`. Eg. `'[a,b]'`, and omitting"
" the space between `key: value` and quoting the key. Eg. `'{\"a\":b}'` "
"Can be useful when using yaml for pretty URL query params as spaces are "
"%-encoded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/js-yaml_README.md:188
msgid ""
"The following table show availlable styles (e.g. \"canonical\", "
"\"binary\"...) available for each tag (.e.g. !!null, !!int ...). Yaml "
"output is shown on the right side after `=>` (default setting) or `->`:"
msgstr ""

